 # Aegis Golden Path (v1)
 
+## OpenClaw integration-critical patch (external tools + approvals + delegation + audit context)
+
+Adds:
+### 1) External tool execution endpoint (strict allowlist + budgets)
+- POST `/v1/external/tools/execute`
+  - requires `client_id`, `tool`, `args`
+  - enforces allowlist per client and budgets per client
+  - requires `approval_id` for high-risk tools
+
+### 2) Approval objects + endpoints
+- POST `/v1/external/approvals` (create request)
+- POST `/v1/external/approvals/{id}/approve`
+- POST `/v1/external/approvals/{id}/deny`
+
+### 3) Tenant delegation policy
+- POST `/v1/external/clients` creates `external_clients` records per tenant:
+  - allowed_tools list
+  - budgets (max_cost_usd, max_minutes)
+
+### 4) Audit schema extension for external context
+`record_audit_event(..., external_context=...)` embeds external context under:
+- `details["_external"] = {channel_id, thread_id, message_id, external_user_id, ...}`
+
+Migrations:
+```bash
+alembic upgrade head
+```
+
+OpenClaw recommended integration:
+1) Create external client for tenant:
+   - allowed_tools = ["signals.prometheus.query","compliance.export","rollout.tick",...]
+2) For high-risk actions:
+   - request approval -> get approval_id -> approve -> execute with approval_id
+3) Always pass external_context JSON (channel/thread ids) for auditability.
+
 ## Agentic upgrade patch: planner + plan graphs + perception + self-correction
